CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
As atomic_symbolic_index_reread, but the re-read is of A[2], the element this
thread has just written: when the other thread runs first, A[2] == 2. A first
version of the fix put the re-read event on the first read generation, which
then had to equal both the value before the write and the value after it, so
the path was dropped and this failure was missed.
